We are interested in finding a ball with the largest possible radius, which is entirely contained within the set P (The center of such a ball is called the Chebychev center of P).", "keywords": ["optimization", "maximization"], "parameters": {"M": {"description": "The number of inequalities defining the set P", "shape": []}, "N": {"description": "The ambient space dimension of the set P", "shape": []}, "A": {"description": "The coefficients of the linear inequalities defining the set P", "shape": ["M", "N"]}, "B": {"description": "The right-hand side of the inequalities defining the set P", "shape": ["M"]}}, "variables": {"Center": {"description": "Coordinates of the center of the ball (Chebyshev center)", "type": "continuous", "shape": ["N"]}, "Radius": {"description": "Radius of the largest inscribed ball", "type": "continuous", "shape": []}}, "constraints": [{"description": "The radius of the ball is non-negative", "formulation": "Radius \geq 0", "code": {"gurobipy": "model.addConstr(Radius >= 0, name="RadiusNonNeg")"}}, {"description": "The ball must be completely within the set P, which is defined by the constraints Ax <= b. For each inequality i, the constraint is a_i^T y + ||a_i|| * r <= b_i.", "formulation": "\sum_{j=0}^{N-1} A_{i,j} \times Center_j + \|a_i\|_2 \times Radius \leq B_i, \quad \forall i \in \{0, \ldots, M-1\}", "code": {"gurobipy": "import math
for i in range(M):
