{"parametrized_description": "The company’s declared objective is to minimize costs. It has K categories of requirements, with each category consisting of I different requirements. The strength of each requirement category is denoted by Strength, whereas the cost reductions per unit less waste in each category and the additional costs per unit more waste in each category are represented by LessOneWaste and MoreOneWaste, respectively. The number of recruits in each category is given by Recruit, and the cost of redundancy per recruit in each category is CostRedundancy. The company can allow NumOverman over-managed categories, with each over-managed category incurring a cost of CostOverman. Similarly, NumShortwork short-work categories are permissible, each one resulting in a cost of CostShort. How should they operate in order to minimize these costs?", "keywords": ["optimization", "minimization"], "parameters": {"K": {"description": "Number of requirements categories", "shape": []}, "I": {"description": "Number of different requirements", "shape": []}, "Strength": {"description": "Strength of each requirement category", "shape": ["K"]}, "LessOneWaste": {"description": "Cost reduction per unit less waste in each category", "shape": ["K"]}, "MoreOneWaste": {"description": "Additional cost per unit more waste in each category", "shape": ["K"]}, "Recruit": {"description": "Number of recruits in each category", "shape": ["K"]}, "CostRedundancy": {"description": "Cost of redundancy per recruit in each category", "shape": ["K"]}, "NumOverman": {"description": "Number of over-managed categories allowed", "shape": []}, "CostOverman": {"description": "Cost of over-managing in each category", "shape": ["K"]}, "NumShortwork": {"description": "Number of short-work categories allowed", "shape": []}, "CostShort": {"description": "Cost of short-work in each category", "shape": ["K"]}, "Requirement": {"description": "Estimated manpower requirements for manpower k in year i", "shape": ["K", "I"]}}, "variables": {"RecruitNum": {"description": "Number of workers recruited in category k in year i", "type": "continuous", "shape": ["K", "I"]}, "Overmanning": {"description": "Number of overmanned workers in category k in year i", "type": "continuous", "shape": ["K", "I"]}, "Short": {"description": "Number of short-time workers in category k in year i", "type": "continuous", "shape": ["K", "I"]}, "Redundancy": {"description": "Number of workers made redundant in category k in year i", "type": "continuous", "shape": ["K", "I"]}}, "constraints": [{"description": "All decision variables must be non-negative", "formulation": "RecruitNum_{k,i} \geq 0, \quad Overmanning_{k,i} \geq 0, \quad Short_{k,i} \geq 0, \quad Redundancy_{k,i} \geq 0, \quad \forall k, i", "code": {"gurobipy": "for k in range(K):
    for i in range(I):
        model.addConstr(RecruitNum[k][i] >= 0, name=f"NonNegRecruit_{k}_{i}")
        model.addConstr(Overmanning[k][i] >= 0, name=f"NonNegOverman_{k}_{i}")
        model.addConstr(Short[k][i] >= 0, name=f"NonNegShort_{k}_{i}")
        model.addConstr(Redundancy[k][i] >= 0, name=f"NonNegRedundancy_{k}_{i}")"}}, {"description": "Recruitment in each category is limited to the maximum recruit number", "formulation": "RecruitNum_{k,i} \leq Recruit_{k}, \quad \forall k, i", "code": {"gurobipy": "for k in range(K):
    for i in range(I):
        model.addConstr(RecruitNum[k][i] <= Recruit[k], name=f"MaxRecruit_{k}_{i}")"}}, {"description": "Short-time working in each category is limited to NumShortwork", "formulation": "Short_{k,i} \leq NumShortwork, \quad \forall k, i", "code": {"gurobipy": "for k in range(K):
    for i in range(I):
        model.addConstr(Short[k][i] <= NumShortwork, name=f"MaxShort_{k}_{i}")"}}, {"description": "Total overmanning across all categories is limited to NumOverman in each year", "formulation": "\sum_{k=1}^{K} Overmanning_{k,i} \leq NumOverman, \quad \forall i", "code": {"gurobipy": "for i in range(I):
    model.addConstr(gurobipy.quicksum(Overmanning[k][i] for k in range(K)) <= NumOverman, name=f"MaxOverman_{i}")"}}, {"description": "Manpower balance: workforce in each category and year equals the requirement plus overmanning minus short-time contribution. First year uses Strength as the starting workforce.", "formulation": "Requirement_{k,i} + Overmanning_{k,i} - 0.5 \times Short_{k,i} = (1 - MoreOneWaste_{k}) \times PreviousWorkforce_{k,i} + (1 - LessOneWaste_{k}) \times RecruitNum_{k,i} - Redundancy_{k,i}, \quad \forall k, i", "code": {"gurobipy": "for k in range(K):
    for i in range(I):
        if i == 0:
            prev_workforce = Strength[k]
        else:
            prev_workforce = Requirement[k][i-1] + Overmanning[k][i-1] - 0.5 * Short[k][i-1]
        model.addConstr(Requirement[k][i] + Overmanning[k][i] - 0.5 * Short[k][i] == (1 - MoreOneWaste[k]) * prev_workforce + (1 - LessOneWaste[k]) * RecruitNum[k][i] - Redundancy[k][i], name=f"Balance_{k}_{i}")"}}], "objective": {"description": "Minimize the overall costs of operations including redundancy, overmanning, and short working", "formulation": "\min \ \sum_{k=1}^{K} \sum_{i=1}^{I} \left( CostRedundancy_{k} \times Redundancy_{k,i} + CostOverman_{k} \times Overmanning_{k,i} + CostShort_{k} \times Short_{k,i} \right)", "code": {"gurobipy": "model.setObjective(gurobipy.quicksum(CostRedundancy[k] * Redundancy[k][i] + CostOverman[k] * Overmanning[k][i] + CostShort[k] * Short[k][i] for k in range(K) for i in range(I)), GRB.MINIMIZE)"}}}

{"parametrized_description": "To maximize profit, which mines should be operated each year and how much should they produce? The company has K mines and can operate at most MaxWork in any given year. For each mine k, there is a royalty cost of Royalty, a production limit of Limit, and the material extracted has a quality of Quality. Each client i requires a material with at least RequiredQuality. The price per unit of material sold is Price, with a discount Discount applied to the royalty cost for each unit sold.", "keywords": ["optimization", "maximization"], "parameters": {"K": {"description": "Number of mines", "shape": []}, "MaxWork": {"description": "Maximum number of mines that can be operated in a year", "shape": []}, "NumYears": {"description": "Number of years the company will be operating", "shape": []}, "Royalty": {"description": "Royalty cost for operating mine k", "shape": ["K"]}, "Limit": {"description": "Production limit for mine k", "shape": ["K"]}, "Quality": {"description": "Quality of the material from mine k", "shape": ["K"]}, "RequiredQuality": {"description": "Required quality of the material for each year", "shape": ["NumYears"]}, "Price": {"description": "Price per unit of material sold", "shape": []}, "Discount": {"description": "Discount rate on the royalty cost per unit of material sold", "shape": []}}, "variables": {"IsOperated": {"description": "Binary variable indicating whether mine k is operated in year i", "type": "integer", "shape": ["K", "NumYears"]}, "Amount": {"description": "Amount of ore produced by mine k in year i", "type": "continuous", "shape": ["K", "NumYears"]}}, "constraints": [{"description": "Number of operated mines does not exceed MaxWork in each year", "formulation": "\sum_{k=1}^{K} IsOperated_{k,i} \leq MaxWork, \quad \forall i \in \{1, \ldots, NumYears\}", "code": {"gurobipy": "for i in range(NumYears):
    model.addConstr(gurobipy.quicksum(IsOperated[k][i] for k in range(K)) <= MaxWork, name=f"MaxMines_{i}")"}}, {"description": "Each mine k produces a non-negative amount of material", "formulation": "Amount_{k,i} \geq 0, \quad \forall k, i", "code": {"gurobipy": "for k in range(K):
    for i in range(NumYears):
        model.addConstr(Amount[k][i] >= 0, name=f"NonNegAmount_{k}_{i}")"}}, {"description": "Each mine k has a production limit of Limit, and can only produce if operated", "formulation": "Amount_{k,i} \leq Limit_{k} \times IsOperated_{k,i}, \quad \forall k, i", "code": {"gurobipy": "for k in range(K):
    for i in range(NumYears):
        model.addConstr(Amount[k][i] <= Limit[k] * IsOperated[k][i], name=f"ProdLimit_{k}_{i}")"}}, {"description": "The blended quality of ore in each year must equal the required quality (weighted average)", "formulation": "\sum_{k=1}^{K} Quality_{k} \times Amount_{k,i} = RequiredQuality_{i} \times \sum_{k=1}^{K} Amount_{k,i}, \quad \forall i", "code": {"gurobipy": "for i in range(NumYears):
    model.addConstr(gurobipy.quicksum(Quality[k] * Amount[k][i] for k in range(K)) == RequiredQuality[i] * gurobipy.quicksum(Amount[k][i] for k in range(K)), name=f"QualityReq_{i}")"}}, {"description": "If a mine is operated in a future year, it must be kept open (operated or maintained) in all previous years", "formulation": "IsOperated_{k,i} \leq IsOperated_{k,i-1}, \quad \forall k, \forall i \geq 2 \quad \text{(once closed, stays closed)}", "code": {"gurobipy": "for k in range(K):
    for i in range(1, NumYears):
        model.addConstr(IsOperated[k][i] <= IsOperated[k][i-1], name=f"OpenContinuity_{k}_{i}")"}}], "objective": {"description": "Maximize the company's discounted profit from operating the mines and selling the material produced", "formulation": "\max \ \sum_{i=1}^{NumYears} \frac{1}{(1 + Discount)^{i}} \left( Price \times \sum_{k=1}^{K} Amount_{k,i} - \sum_{k=1}^{K} Royalty_{k} \times IsOperated_{k,i} \right)", "code": {"gurobipy": "model.setObjective(gurobipy.quicksum((1 / (1 + Discount) ** (i + 1)) * (Price * gurobipy.quicksum(Amount[k][i] for k in range(K)) - gurobipy.quicksum(Royalty[k] * IsOperated[k][i] for k in range(K))) for i in range(NumYears)), GRB.MAXIMIZE)"}}}

{"parametrized_description": "Maximize total productive capacity at the end of the five years. The problem parameters are a matrix of coefficients InputOne, a vector of manpower coefficients for input one ManpowerOne, a matrix of coefficients InputTwo, a vector of manpower coefficients for input two ManpowerTwo, initial stock levels Stock, productive capacities Capacity, a company-wide manpower limit ManpowerLimit, and demand for each productive unit Demand.", "keywords": ["optimization", "maximization"], "parameters": {"NumYears": {"description": "Total number of years in the planning horizon", "shape": []}, "NumIndustries": {"description": "Total number of industries", "shape": []}, "InputOne": {"description": "Input one coefficients matrix", "shape": ["NumIndustries", "NumIndustries"]}, "ManpowerOne": {"description": "Manpower coefficients for input one", "shape": ["NumIndustries"]}, "InputTwo": {"description": "Input two coefficients matrix", "shape": ["NumIndustries", "NumIndustries"]}, "ManpowerTwo": {"description": "Manpower coefficients for input two", "shape": ["NumIndustries"]}, "Stock": {"description": "Initial stock level for each of the productive units", "shape": ["NumIndustries"]}, "Capacity": {"description": "Productive capacity for each productive unit", "shape": ["NumIndustries"]}, "ManpowerLimit": {"description": "Company-wide manpower limit", "shape": []}, "Demand": {"description": "Demand for each of the productive units at the end of the planning horizon", "shape": ["NumIndustries"]}}, "variables": {"Produce": {"description": "Amount of units produced by industry k in year t", "type": "continuous", "shape": ["NumIndustries", "NumYears"]}, "BuildCapa": {"description": "Amount of units used to build productive capacity for industry k in year t", "type": "continuous", "shape": ["NumIndustries", "NumYears"]}, "StockHold": {"description": "Amount of stock of industry k held at end of year t", "type": "continuous", "shape": ["NumIndustries", "NumYears"]}}, "constraints": [{"description": "There is a company-wide manpower limit denoted by ManpowerLimit", "formulation": "\sum_{k=1}^{NumIndustries} ManpowerOne_{k} \times Produce_{k,t} + \sum_{k=1}^{NumIndustries} ManpowerTwo_{k} \times BuildCapa_{k,t} \leq ManpowerLimit, \quad \forall t \in \{1, \ldots, NumYears\}", "code": {"gurobipy": "for t in range(NumYears):
    model.addConstr(quicksum(ManpowerOne[k] * Produce[k][t] for k in range(NumIndustries)) + quicksum(ManpowerTwo[k] * BuildCapa[k][t] for k in range(NumIndustries)) <= ManpowerLimit, name=f"ManpowerLimit_{t}")"}}, {"description": "The production must meet certain demand levels specified by Demand", "formulation": "Produce_{k,t} + StockHold_{k,t-1} - StockHold_{k,t} - \sum_{j=1}^{NumIndustries} InputOne_{j,k} \times Produce_{j,t} - \sum_{j=1}^{NumIndustries} InputTwo_{j,k} \times BuildCapa_{j,t} \geq Demand_{k}, \quad \forall k \in \{1, \ldots, NumIndustries\}, \forall t \in \{1, \ldots, NumYears\}", "code": {"gurobipy": "for k in range(NumIndustries):
    for t in range(NumYears):
        stock_prev = Stock[k] if t == 0 else StockHold[k][t-1]
        model.addConstr(Produce[k][t] + stock_prev - StockHold[k][t] - quicksum(InputOne[j][k] * Produce[j][t] for j in range(NumIndustries)) - quicksum(InputTwo[j][k] * BuildCapa[j][t] for j in range(NumIndustries)) >= Demand[k], name=f"Demand_{k}_{t}")"}}, {"description": "Production cannot exceed productive capacity, which increases based on past capacity building", "formulation": "Produce_{k,t} \leq Capacity_{k} + \sum_{t'=1}^{t-2} BuildCapa_{k,t'}, \quad \forall k \in \{1, \ldots, NumIndustries\}, \forall t \in \{1, \ldots, NumYears\}", "code": {"gurobipy": "for k in range(NumIndustries):
    for t in range(NumYears):
        if t <= 1:
            model.addConstr(Produce[k][t] <= Capacity[k], name=f"CapLimit_{k}_{t}")
        else:
            model.addConstr(Produce[k][t] <= Capacity[k] + quicksum(BuildCapa[k][tp] for tp in range(t-1)), name=f"CapLimit_{k}_{t}")"}}, {"description": "Each input usage and productive capacity must be non-negative", "formulation": "Produce_{k,t} \geq 0, \quad BuildCapa_{k,t} \geq 0, \quad StockHold_{k,t} \geq 0, \quad \forall k, t", "code": {"gurobipy": "for k in range(NumIndustries):
    for t in range(NumYears):
        model.addConstr(Produce[k][t] >= 0, name=f"ProdNonNeg_{k}_{t}")
        model.addConstr(BuildCapa[k][t] >= 0, name=f"BuildNonNeg_{k}_{t}")
        model.addConstr(StockHold[k][t] >= 0, name=f"StockNonNeg_{k}_{t}")"}}], "objective": {"description": "Maximize total productive capacity at the end of the five years", "formulation": "\max \sum_{k=1}^{NumIndustries} \left( Capacity_{k} + \sum_{t=1}^{NumYears-1} BuildCapa_{k,t} \right)", "code": {"gurobipy": "model.setObjective(quicksum(Capacity[k] + quicksum(BuildCapa[k][t] for t in range(NumYears - 1)) for k in range(NumIndustries)), GRB.MAXIMIZE)"}}}

